# Isolated v2 cleanup SQL implementation notes

New repository file only: `docs/pilot/conversation/sql-drafts/p5-voice-v2-cleanup.sql`.

The isolated draft adds one nullable `protocol` column to the existing shared `cleanup_owners` table. Existing rows and explicit-column writers retain NULL; new v2 registration writes exactly 2 with complete nonnil Auth-session/parent-version/fingerprint binding. The new CHECK rejects other protocol values and incomplete v2 bindings. No third sidecar, duplicate accounting, backfill, migration, runtime route or legacy source change is introduced.

Two new service-only RPCs are installed in the same transaction as revocation of their default access. Their private observation helper is not executable by service_role, anon or authenticated. Existing privileges are not modified.

- `bfa_p5_v2_register_cleanup(p_cleanup_id uuid,p_claim jsonb,p_auth_session_id uuid,p_parent_version bigint,p_fingerprint text,p_verified_ms bigint,p_auth_expires_ms bigint)`.
- `bfa_p5_v2_read_cleanup(p_cleanup_id uuid,p_claim jsonb,p_auth_session_id uuid,p_parent_version bigint,p_fingerprint text)`.

Both use the existing strict claim parser and additionally reject every nil UUID, plus unsafe versions/timing and invalid fingerprints. The common exclusive owner lock precedes row locks. Registration checks the exact clear current Auth parent/version, excludes every retained v1 session row for that pair, checks current protected allowlist/thread/generation, and requires the exact existing protocol-2 issuance association. Existing cleanup must already be the same complete v2 binding and claim with no terminal field; legacy/unbound, mismatched or terminal rows are denied without adoption or repair.

Registration remains pre-proof/pre-admission: any retained proof at cleanup ID or claim ID, shared claim row at claim ID, or owner/attempt row denies it. It never modifies those records or their accounting. Current approval/quota admission is deliberately a later stage, not conferred here.

Clock sampling occurs after all row locks. Unsafe/rollback time or future verifiedAt denies before cleanup mutation. An exact existing eligible row may retain a shorter deadline from safe, nonfuture metadata even if verification aged during waits: min of original effective expiry, exact claim, issuance, Auth and finite allowlist. This is negative evidence only. Original verification age >=30000 ms or a deadline at/before now denies success and never inserts a new row. New records require fresh verifiedAt and all positive eligibility. A later longer observation cannot extend a retained deadline. Equal/longer deadlines do not issue a no-op UPDATE. Registration changes only owner-clock high-water plus absent cleanup insertion or exact cleanup deadline shortening; no expired/invalidated timestamp is fabricated.

Read returns only an exact persisted v2 association, including all nullable terminal timestamps. It uses no clock, current parent/issuance/allowlist/thread eligibility checks or writes. It stays usable after expiry, revocation, closure or deletion as server-only evidence; NULL never proves absence, and a nonterminal observation is never current Auth or admission. Request/reply association and independently verified Auth policy remain mandatory trusted-host requirements, not established by service-role access or metadata shape.

Existing exact close creates or preserves terminal NULL-protocol cleanup before registration, which v2 denies. Closing a v2 cleanup preserves its v2 binding and cannot refund holds. The additive column is compatible with existing explicit-column cleanup registration/close and fixture inserts; no positional cleanup INSERT was found in docs/src/scripts/supabase. Old proof/claim/capacity paths still lack v2 provenance enforcement and remain unsuitable for v2 use. Full versioned predicates and quiesced no-fallback cutover are unfinished; this slice is inactive and nondeployable.

Pretest self-review correction: the first draft selected unqualified thread `id` while declaring local claim `id`. It was qualified as `th.id` before completed behavioral testing to avoid PL/pgSQL ambiguity. A separate refinement avoids rewriting an unchanged cleanup row. No existing source or SQL changed.

Current SQL SHA256: `c0a345fe9bc8232e52fde4638a8c57bbcf0a41ea1320d87f246374455fdccd6c`.

The corrected actual SQL integration suite passes 56/56 at this checkpoint; its initial 54/56 failures were fixture-only (a direct deletion mutation violated an existing P3b constraint, and legacy inspect correctly returns claimed rather than the fixture's expected replayed). Additional direct CHECK/preexisting-row preservation cases are being added by the test owner before that fixture freezes. Independent source review found no blocker in the final hash above. The SQL source is frozen; root evidence owns final counts and integrated checks. No connected database or real Auth/provider/device calls occurred.


