# Inactive v2 cleanup transport and primary fixtures — 3 November 2026

Owned repository changes are only the new `src/lib/ai/conversation/service/voice-v2-cleanup-rpc.server.ts` and `src/lib/ai/conversation/__tests__/p5-voice-v2-cleanup-rpc.test.ts`. No prior source, test, SQL, configuration, dependency, runtime route or connected service changed.

The factory exposes exactly `registerCleanup` and `readCleanup`, with a captured protected transport and no default SDK/client/clock. Registration maps the exact preallocated cleanup/claim, actual Auth session, parent version, associated issuance fingerprint, conservative verification time and current Auth-policy ceiling to the agreed v2 RPC. Read maps only the exact persisted association. Both strictly validate protocol 2, every nested immutable claim field and all association fields, and detach/freeze requests and receipts through the nested claim binding. Accessors, inherited identity, symbols/hidden fields, nil or noncanonical UUIDs, unsafe/coercible numbers, extras and wrong digests/scope are rejected.

Registration accepts only a nonterminal response with an effective deadline after the original verification time and no later than the claim/Auth ceilings. SQL remains responsible for locked current time, freshness, parent/legacy/issuance/thread/allowlist checks and any permitted retained shortening on denial. Read has no local clock/current-Auth requirement and accepts retained closed/expired/invalidated timestamps as content-free evidence only. An elapsed effective deadline can still be reported on read; no inference of eligibility or a synthesized state is made.

Null remains semantic denial, never proof of absence or rollback. Thrown or malformed replies produce the fixed sanitized error without cause/identity. No retry, fallback, replacement claim, identity allocation, close, accounting refund or provider call exists. The trusted host must retain exact uncertain request evidence before invocation. Verification time/Auth ceiling are not echoed, so exact invocation/reply association remains a protected nonretrying transport precondition. Shapes and service-role transport establish neither participant Auth nor service provenance. Full v2 proof/admission/capacity and quiesced no-fallback cutover remain unfinished.

First completed focused run: **44/44 passed**. Full `tsc --noEmit`: exit 0. Scoped ESLint for both new files: exit 0. Formatting was applied before these checks. No initial test/type/lint failure or implementation correction occurred in this task. Logs: `adapter-primary-initial.log`, `adapter-typecheck-initial.log`, `adapter-lint-initial.log` alongside this note. Independent composition and actual SQL fixtures are separate; root owns final complete-suite/build/source-preservation checks.

The fixture covers exact wire mappings, nested immutable snapshots, input mutation while pending, mismatching late replies, transport-owned response mutation after return, captured bound client methods, semantic-null denial, no retries and sanitized lost-write errors. It checks terminal read versus active registration, safe numeric boundaries and shrink-only response bounds, all claim identity comparisons, mixed/missing protocol, null-prototype records and rejected request/response/envelope accessors. Transport success metadata is not current eligibility. No actual Auth/provider/network fault or native concurrency evidence is claimed.


