# Independent v2 cleanup review — 3 November 2026

Base: connected main `f88acbca46ef5c8a48a694d84099cc2179fa35db`. Read AGENTS, the latest continuation block and lifetime-change contract, then the existing admission/capacity SQL, v2 parent/issuance/pre-issuance SQL and transport, and unchanged v1 store admission bridge. Reviewed both new cleanup SQL and transport in full. No existing source, SQL, tests, dependencies, configuration or connected service changed by this reviewer.

## Source review

No blocking defect found in the reviewed draft. The shared cleanup table gains only a nullable protocol discriminator. Legacy rows and explicit-column writers retain NULL; v2 records require protocol 2 plus a nonnil complete Auth association. The CHECK avoids SQL NULL passing for its nullable binding members through explicit nonnull tests. The existing table already bounds persisted scalar expiry/terminal values. Initial effective expiry is bounded by the writer, later writers only shorten it, and the strict adapter independently rejects effective expiry above the exact claim expiry.

Registration uses the common exclusive owner advisory lock, then current parent/legacy, staging, thread/generation, issuance and its v2 association, exact cleanup and downstream-record checks before sampling retained owner time. The shared claim parser plus new nil-identity checks establish exact wire shape, canonical identity and integer bounds. Existing cleanup with a different key/claim/binding/protocol or any terminal marker denies; no legacy adoption or rebinding occurs. Any proof for the same cleanup or claim, existing claim, or retained owner/attempt row denies this pre-proof/pre-admission registrar. This keeps later accounting and lifetime changes outside this slice.

For an exact existing row, a valid shorter ceiling is retained even when original verification ages while waiting or the deadline expires; semantic denial does not erase negative evidence. Safe monotonic time and nonfuture verification precede that mutation, as do exact current provenance checks. New rows require full freshness strictly below 30000 ms and positive remaining lifetime. There is no expiry-marker synthesis; persisted expiry remains evidence interpreted by future eligibility gates. No claims, attempts, quotas, proofs, capacity or usage rows are changed by registration.

The exact read takes only content-free retained association identity, returns only matching protocol-2 persisted metadata, and neither samples time nor looks up current Auth eligibility. It can return records after closure, expiry, parent/legacy revocation or thread deletion. This is deliberately reconciliation evidence, never admission or continued permission. Default new-function privileges are revoked in the same transaction; only the two public RPCs gain service execution. The observation helper and private tables remain inaccessible to participant and service roles directly.

The adapter uses strict own-enumerable-data schemas before cross-field checks, detached/frozen nested claims, one captured nonretrying transport call and sanitized errors. It compares the complete claim and association, rejects v1/unbound/malformed replies, bounds a positive registration receipt by supplied verification/Auth expiry, and allows terminal read metadata without a local clock. The omitted verification/Auth fields require trusted exact invocation/reply association. A null result never proves absence or rollback.

The SQL author corrected a local-variable/thread-column `id` ambiguity during source review before behavioral execution and removed unnecessary same-value expiry updates. These were new-draft-only corrections. Root and the SQL-test owner record final execution, hashes and any further findings separately.

